OpenCode offers multiple ways to access AI models: OpenCode Zen : a pay-as-you-go subscription with access to a large number of tested and verified models OpenCode Zen Free : free access to a limited set of models, with data and feedback collected to improve the models OpenCode Go : a low-cost monthly subscription with access to a validated set of open coding models Visit OpenCode Console and create an account Free models are available without payment. To use Zen or Go models, make sure you have enough credits or an active subscription Generate an API key from the "API Keys" section in the OpenCode Console Open the settings view (agent: open settings) and go to the OpenCode section Enter your OpenCode API key The OpenCode API key will be saved in your keychain. Zed will also use the OPENCODE_API_KEY environment variable if it's defined. By default, models from all subscription types are shown. Optionally, you can hide subscriptions that are not relevant to you by clicking the toggles or by adding the following to your settings: { "language_models": { "opencode": { "show_zen_models": true, "show_go_models": false, "show_free_models": false } }
